# WHICH Aether release bootstrap.sh installs when AETHER_PIN is not met.
#
# Separate from AETHER_PIN on purpose, and the split is the whole point:
#
#   AETHER_PIN    a FLOOR — the oldest Aether that can compile this repo.
#                 Moves only when a new call needs a newer primitive.
#                 Someone already above the floor is left alone.
#
#   AETHER_FETCH  a KNOWN-GOOD release to actually download. Moves for
#                 reasons unrelated to language features — toolchain
#                 portability, a fixed codegen bug, a release whose
#                 assets are all published. A newer number here is not
#                 automatically better; it is another thing to have
#                 tested.
#
# MUST BE >= AETHER_PIN. This names the release we DOWNLOAD when the pin
# is unsatisfied, so a value below the floor would install a toolchain
# that cannot build this repo — the fetch would "succeed" and the build
# would then fail deep in a generated C file, which is exactly the
# confusion the pin exists to prevent.
#
# --- Why 0.542.0 (2026-08-15) ---
#
# Verified locally: `ae 0.542.0` builds build/f3, build/fight_flash_fraud
# and both spec binaries, and tests/unit passes 4/4 against the stdlib
# std.spec with no aeocha checkout anywhere on AETHER_LIB_DIR.
#
# Sibling projects for cross-reference — aeb pins its own machinery at
# 0.541.0, aether-ui tracks the release line and has already migrated its
# whole spec suite to std.spec.
#
# NB on glibc, inherited from aeb's notes and still worth knowing: Aether
# releases up to ~0.449 were built on ubuntu-latest and carry a
# GLIBC_2.38 floor, so `aetherc` dies on Debian 12 (glibc 2.36) while
# `ae --version` still works — a version-only probe reports a healthy
# toolchain that cannot build. Aether's release.yml now pins ubuntu-22.04
# (glibc 2.35). That concern belongs to THIS file, not the pin: it is
# about which release to fetch, not what the floor is.
#
# --- Raised 0.542.0 -> 0.737.0 (2026-09-29) ---
#
# Verified locally on macOS/arm64: `ae 0.737.0` builds build/f3,
# build/fight_flash_fraud and both spec binaries; tests/unit passes 4/4
# and tests/ui (over AetherUIDriver) passes 2/2. AETHER_PIN is UNCHANGED
# (0.538.0) -- nothing here started needing a newer primitive, so this is
# purely "what to fetch," not a floor move.
#
# The GUI build DID need a real fix, but it was aether-ui's drift, not
# aether's: scripts/build-ui.sh's macOS link line was missing
# `-framework CoreText -framework ImageIO -framework OpenGL` (gpuview's
# GL context and friends, added to aether-ui's own canonical darwin link
# set since this repo's build-ui.sh was last synced with it) and failed
# with undefined `_glBindFramebuffer` and friends until those three were
# added. If a future aether-ui pulls in another framework the same way,
# this script needs a matching update again -- it hand-duplicates
# aether-ui's link flags rather than sharing them (see README's
# "why a source checkout" section), so it can drift independently of
# whatever Aether release is pinned here.
#
# 0.766.0 (2026-10-03): equals AETHER_PIN, the family-wide floor. Verified as
# AETHER_PIN describes.
#
# 0.778.0 (2026-10-05): a TRACKING bump with AETHER_PIN, not a new-primitive
# floor. Verified on the released 0.778.0 with the full suite, as AETHER_PIN
# describes.
